+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are skipped unless the `-l/--links`
+flag is in use. With `--links` they are exposed as regular files with a
+`.rclonelink` suffix whose contents are the target of the link, in the
+same way as the [local backend](/local/#symlinks-junction-points). This means
+`rclone copy --links` recreates them as symlinks on a destination which
+supports them.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular archive member whose name happens to end in `.rclonelink` is
+treated as a regular file, and takes precedence over a symlink of the
+same name.
+
